  <description>&lt;p&gt;In recent weeks, AI has solved hundreds of previously unanswered maths problems. Our correspondents ask if machines can do the same in other areas of &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/leaders/2026/10/15/what-if-the-machines-take-over-science?utm_campaign=a.io&amp;utm_medium=audio.podcast.np&amp;utm_source=theintelligence&amp;utm_content=discovery.content.anonymous.tr_shownotes_na-na_article&amp;utm_term=sa.listeners&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;science&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and what role human researchers may play. Why crisps are getting &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/business/2026/10/08/why-your-snacks-are-chunkier-and-chewier-than-before?utm_campaign=a.io&amp;utm_medium=audio.podcast.np&amp;utm_source=theintelligence&amp;utm_content=discovery.content.anonymous.tr_shownotes_na-na_article&amp;utm_term=sa.listeners&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;chunkier&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and chocolate chewier. And celebrating the life and work of author &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/obituary/2026/10/15/annie-dillard-wanted-to-know-the-mind-of-god?utm_campaign=a.io&amp;utm_medium=audio.podcast.np&amp;utm_source=theintelligence&amp;utm_content=discovery.content.anonymous.tr_shownotes_na-na_article&amp;utm_term=sa.listeners&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Annie Dillard&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Watch extended clips from Insider &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/interactive/insider/previews?utm_campaign=a.brand_fy2627_q1_awareness-imp-tr_prospecting_global-global_direct_na&amp;utm_medium=audio.podcast.pd&amp;utm_source=economist&amp;utm_content=discovery.awareness.anonymous.tr_nativeread_np-tiinsider-apr_na-na_web_na_na_na_na&amp;utm_term=sa.arc-isi&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Guests and host:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Alex Hern, AI writer&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Alok Jha, science editor&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Avantika Chilkoti, global business writer&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ann Wroe, obituaries editor&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Rosie Blau, co-host of “The Intelligence”&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Jason Palmer, co-host of “The Intelligence”&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Topics covered: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scientific research, mathpocalypse, AI &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Crisps, snacks, texture, crunchtok&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Annie Dillard, nature, obituary&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Listen to what matters most, from global politics and business to science and technology—&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://subscribenow.economist.com/podcasts-plus&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;subscribe to The Economist&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;p style=&apos;color:grey; font-size:0.75em;&apos;&gt; Hosted on Acast. See &lt;a style=&apos;color:grey;&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos; rel=&apos;noopener noreferrer&apos; href=&apos;https://acast.com/privacy&apos;&gt;acast.com/privacy&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
